WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.021
are inspired by a true story.

00:00:03.021 --> 00:00:05.954
Names, dates, and details
have been changed.

00:00:05.954 --> 00:00:07.787
Viewer discretion is advised.

00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:13.120
Town sweetheart goes missing
and everyone is a suspect.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.153
Could it be the married man
she was seeing on the side?

00:00:16.153 --> 00:00:17.454
The irate customer

00:00:17.454 --> 00:00:19.721
who won't take no for an answer.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:23.220
And why is her brother being so
helpful?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.021
When every new avenue leads to a
dead end,

00:00:26.021 --> 00:00:29.988
police will have to put this
puzzle together piece by piece.

00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:34.287
(perky music)

00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:40.621
(man gasps)

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:43.287
(blade scrapes)

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.854
(head thuds)

00:01:03.088 --> 00:01:05.854
Appleton, Wisconsin, 2007.

00:01:06.687 --> 00:01:11.088
Gloria McClain had long been
Appleton's pride and joy.

00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:13.721
Having spent the majority of her
childhood

00:01:13.721 --> 00:01:16.721
on a semi-popular 1990's sitcom,

00:01:16.721 --> 00:01:20.988
she was as close to
celebrity as many in her town

00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:22.287
would ever encounter.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.954
After her stardom faded,

00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:29.287
Gloria returned to Appleton
to attempt a new life.

00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:32.721
She graduated from school with
top honors

00:01:32.721 --> 00:01:35.754
and eventually settled into a
new job

00:01:35.754 --> 00:01:39.587
running the loans department
of the Appleton Savings Bank.

00:01:40.787 --> 00:01:43.587
Even when her life was
going at a meager pace,

00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:47.387
she continued to be the
favored daughter of her town.

00:01:48.253 --> 00:01:51.954
So, everyone in Appleton
was quick to notice

00:01:51.954 --> 00:01:55.587
when Gloria went missing.

00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:57.354
- When somebody who's very loved

00:01:57.354 --> 00:01:59.120
in a community goes missing,

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.120
it's not surprising that
people wanna come out and help

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.387
and they come out in droves.

00:02:03.387 --> 00:02:05.654
But the problem you have with
that

00:02:05.654 --> 00:02:08.821
is that sometimes they're not
doing things that the police

00:02:08.821 --> 00:02:10.153
would actually have them do

00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:13.921
and it causes more
problems than it does help.

00:02:13.921 --> 00:02:16.621
- [Narrator] After two nights
of Gloria's absence at home,

00:02:16.621 --> 00:02:20.021
her brother, Paul McClain
files a missing persons report

00:02:20.021 --> 00:02:22.021
to the local authorities.

00:02:22.021 --> 00:02:24.454
- Okay, your sister,
what is her first name?

00:02:24.454 --> 00:02:26.887
- [Narrator] Paul McClain
managed to be everything

00:02:26.887 --> 00:02:28.887
that Gloria was not.

00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:31.954
After a prank on his
sister went horribly wrong,

00:02:31.954 --> 00:02:33.954
Paul sustained a back injury

00:02:33.954 --> 00:02:37.954
that made his confidence take a
nosedive.

00:02:37.954 --> 00:02:40.088
He could no longer play sports

00:02:40.088 --> 00:02:42.988
and school did not come easy for
him.

00:02:42.988 --> 00:02:47.554
He began to isolate himself,
obsessing over Japanese anime,

00:02:47.554 --> 00:02:50.587
and spending his free time

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:54.220
testing new combinations of
sodas.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.721
(bell rings)

00:02:55.721 --> 00:02:58.587
Knowing he was the ridicule of
the town,

00:02:58.587 --> 00:03:00.721
Paul sought to prove everyone
wrong

00:03:00.721 --> 00:03:03.054
by attending the local community
college,

00:03:03.054 --> 00:03:07.153
but at a much more deliberately
slow pace.

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:10.921
Since Gloria and Paul's parents
died,

00:03:10.921 --> 00:03:13.887
the two have lived in
the old family house.

00:03:13.887 --> 00:03:17.387
Gloria always worried about
her brother's financial state,

00:03:17.387 --> 00:03:20.253
and since the house had
already been paid off,

00:03:20.253 --> 00:03:24.520
it was easier for the two to
just continue living there

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.387
until Paul graduated college, of
course.

00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:34.187
Paul reports Gloria missing
with great concern and distress.

00:03:34.187 --> 00:03:37.621
When asked if he knows of anyone
who might kidnap his sister

00:03:37.621 --> 00:03:42.354
he responds with one name,
Darren Tooley.

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:44.187
- Anytime anybody goes missing,

00:03:44.187 --> 00:03:46.787
the first thing detectives
are gonna focus on

00:03:46.787 --> 00:03:48.954
is that person's inner circle.

00:03:48.954 --> 00:03:50.454
The second thing they're gonna
do

00:03:50.454 --> 00:03:53.754
is try to whittle down
the list of suspects

00:03:53.754 --> 00:03:57.021
but Darren is not gonna
get marked off this list.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.387
- [Narrator] Detective
Diana Cox leads the case

00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:06.387
and begins turning her
attention towards Darren Tooley.

00:04:06.921 --> 00:04:10.721
Police learn that Darren is
an artist and local celebrity,

00:04:10.721 --> 00:04:14.187
often found painting in the
middle of the town park.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.587
Darren has also been married to
his wife,

00:04:16.587 --> 00:04:18.287
Joanna for 10 years.

00:04:18.287 --> 00:04:19.821
She's a real estate agent,

00:04:19.821 --> 00:04:23.454
and recently, he and Darren
have not been seen together

00:04:23.454 --> 00:04:26.220
in public for quite some time.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.253
Now detectives understand why
that is.

00:04:29.253 --> 00:04:33.487
Paul believes Darren has been
having an affair with Gloria.

00:04:39.587 --> 00:04:42.887
While Detective Cox began
tracking down Darren Tooley,

00:04:42.887 --> 00:04:45.454
Paul starts making missing
person fliers

00:04:45.454 --> 00:04:47.354
to help find his sister.

00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:49.687
Police are skeptical of Paul's
efforts.

00:04:49.687 --> 00:04:51.187
The town has long considered

00:04:51.187 --> 00:04:55.120
Gloria and Paul's
relationship, a rocky one.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.287
Paul's guilt at holding his
sister back

00:04:57.287 --> 00:04:59.153
only amplifies the fact

00:04:59.153 --> 00:05:03.054
that he constantly lives
in Gloria's shadow.

00:05:03.054 --> 00:05:05.587
It's difficult to tell
if Paul is doing this

00:05:05.587 --> 00:05:10.220
out of love for his sibling
or just a familial obligation.

00:05:13.687 --> 00:05:17.088
Detective Cox arrives early
to Darren Tooley's house

00:05:17.088 --> 00:05:20.654
and finds his wife Joanna
relatively at peace

00:05:20.654 --> 00:05:24.387
as though she is entirely
unaware of the possibility

00:05:24.387 --> 00:05:27.387
her husband could be cheating on
her.

00:05:27.387 --> 00:05:30.287
Joanna tells Detective
Cox that Darren was headed

00:05:30.287 --> 00:05:32.854
towards Gordon Bubolz Nature
Preserve

00:05:32.854 --> 00:05:35.887
but that's not out of
the ordinary for him.

00:05:35.887 --> 00:05:38.253
- If you have a friend who
comes up to you and says,

00:05:38.253 --> 00:05:40.420
I need to disappear without a
trace

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.320
for a long period of
time, raise the red flag

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.821
if it hasn't already been
raised for you, that's strange.

00:05:46.821 --> 00:05:50.120
And Darren decides that he has
to do that.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.787
I bet he's finding some pretty
good inspiration elsewhere,

00:05:52.787 --> 00:05:53.621
don't you think?

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.120
- [Narrator] Detective Cox sets
out

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.554
for Gordon Bubolz Nature
Preserve

00:05:58.554 --> 00:06:01.487
but she finds that Darren is
not listed among the campers

00:06:01.487 --> 00:06:03.487
at the park's registration.

00:06:03.487 --> 00:06:06.988
She returns to the
station with a new idea.

00:06:06.988 --> 00:06:10.054
She goes through Gloria's
credit card payment history

00:06:10.054 --> 00:06:12.420
as well as her recent phone
calls,

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.587
but there is nothing out of the
ordinary

00:06:14.587 --> 00:06:17.520
that Cox finds worthwhile to
investigate.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.821
Later that day, Paul McClain
returns to the station

00:06:23.821 --> 00:06:25.420
after one of his classes

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.921
to infer how the investigation
is going.

00:06:30.887 --> 00:06:34.687
Detective Cox gives him the
only theory she can compose.

00:06:34.687 --> 00:06:36.954
She believes that Gloria and
Darren

00:06:36.954 --> 00:06:38.887
have likely run off together.

00:06:38.887 --> 00:06:41.088
She explains that with no
evidence,

00:06:41.088 --> 00:06:45.354
no body and no witnesses,
it is difficult to assess

00:06:45.354 --> 00:06:48.854
whether Gloria ran away or was
kidnapped.

00:06:48.854 --> 00:06:51.587
- When you're dealing with the
family of a missing person,

00:06:51.587 --> 00:06:54.754
the amount of information
you give them is critical.

00:06:54.754 --> 00:06:59.287
Nobody needs to remind Paul
what the other option is.

00:06:59.287 --> 00:07:00.454
- It's gonna be all right.

00:07:00.454 --> 00:07:02.054
- She could be gone.
- Listen, Paul.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.253
- [Narrator] Paul becomes
visibly upset,

00:07:04.253 --> 00:07:06.721
claiming the Gloria would never
run away

00:07:06.721 --> 00:07:08.887
so long as she had to take care
of him

00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:11.187
while he was getting through
college.

00:07:11.187 --> 00:07:13.921
Detective Cox does her best to
control

00:07:13.921 --> 00:07:17.253
Paul's explosive temper
and tells him to continue

00:07:17.253 --> 00:07:21.220
trying to call Gloria
over the next few days.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.253
Paul leaves disgruntled,
but not at a complete loss.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.120
(phone ringing)

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.854
Later that day, Detective
Cox receives a call

00:07:31.854 --> 00:07:33.754
from someone in Memorial Park,

00:07:33.754 --> 00:07:36.387
claiming that they found
a suspicious package

00:07:36.387 --> 00:07:40.021
that they believe police
should investigate.

00:07:40.021 --> 00:07:43.587
Police arrive on the scene to
discover a sizeable suitcase

00:07:43.587 --> 00:07:45.988
lying near a large electrical
tower

00:07:45.988 --> 00:07:47.487
and river creek.

00:07:47.487 --> 00:07:49.887
Carefully, they pop it open,

00:07:49.887 --> 00:07:54.887
only to find a sight that
sickens them to their stomachs.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.921
Detective Cox pops open
the lid of the suitcase

00:08:01.921 --> 00:08:05.187
and finds a woman's naked torso.

00:08:05.187 --> 00:08:07.988
After they recover from the
ghastly sight,

00:08:07.988 --> 00:08:12.054
they quickly bring in the body
to test it for fingerprints

00:08:12.054 --> 00:08:16.621
or some kind of identification,
but they find neither.

00:08:18.988 --> 00:08:21.687
With no security cameras
surveilling the area,

00:08:21.687 --> 00:08:23.854
police question nearby
witnesses,

00:08:23.854 --> 00:08:28.520
but nobody claims to have seen
who dropped off the suitcase.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.187
And many note, the smell kept
most of them

00:08:31.187 --> 00:08:32.988
from even approaching it.

00:08:32.988 --> 00:08:35.520
Police then ask if they know who
it was

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.721
that called them to the scene,

00:08:37.721 --> 00:08:41.220
but no one steps forward
claiming they did so.

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:42.921
- Zero.

00:08:46.687 --> 00:08:49.253
- [Narrator] Detective
warrants a search of Gloria

00:08:49.253 --> 00:08:53.220
and Paul's home hoping to
find either DNA evidence

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.420
or something else to give them a
lead.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.021
But when Cox arrives,

00:08:59.021 --> 00:09:03.988
she discovers that all of
glorious suitcases are gone

00:09:03.988 --> 00:09:06.887
and that the entire house has
been cleaned

00:09:06.887 --> 00:09:10.554
from top to bottom except for
Paul's room,

00:09:10.554 --> 00:09:13.654
which is a total mess.

00:09:13.654 --> 00:09:17.088
Paul tells Cox that
Gloria was a neat freak.

00:09:17.088 --> 00:09:19.721
And the week before she
disappeared,

00:09:19.721 --> 00:09:23.621
she spent nearly all
her time spring cleaning

00:09:23.621 --> 00:09:28.621
the entire house but he
didn't let her touch his room.

00:09:28.921 --> 00:09:33.520
Cox is astounded as she's
unable to find any DNA

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:35.787
that could possibly help
identify

00:09:35.787 --> 00:09:40.787
if the torso in the suitcase
belonged to Gloria or not.

00:09:41.153 --> 00:09:43.554
They search her bathroom for
toiletries,

00:09:43.554 --> 00:09:46.621
but found that they have been
cleared out.

00:09:46.621 --> 00:09:50.120
Cox asked Paul if he ever
saw her packing her suitcase

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.687
but Paul claims he never saw
anything

00:09:52.687 --> 00:09:56.054
that would suggest she
was going traveling.

00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:59.487
- Detectives have just
found a torso in a suitcase.

00:09:59.487 --> 00:10:00.821
This is either somebody

00:10:00.821 --> 00:10:03.621
who's too good at faking their
own death,

00:10:03.621 --> 00:10:06.054
or it's a murder victim.

00:10:06.054 --> 00:10:08.554
They have obviously the torso's
DNA,

00:10:08.554 --> 00:10:10.754
but there's no match with any
database.

00:10:10.754 --> 00:10:14.887
So they have no idea who this
person was.

00:10:14.887 --> 00:10:17.187
- [Narrator] Not wanting
the investigation stalled,

00:10:17.187 --> 00:10:18.654
Paul tells Detective Cox

00:10:18.654 --> 00:10:20.587
that he remembers hearing his
sister

00:10:20.587 --> 00:10:24.054
complaining about a customer
she had at the bank.

00:10:24.054 --> 00:10:27.220
The customer was screaming
at the top of his lungs

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.954
and making a big scene.

00:10:32.487 --> 00:10:34.921
Detective Cox visits Gloria's
bank

00:10:34.921 --> 00:10:37.054
and pulls up a list of customers

00:10:37.054 --> 00:10:40.088
that she had previously denied
loans to.

00:10:40.088 --> 00:10:43.387
There she finds the name of Tim
Sparks

00:10:43.387 --> 00:10:45.687
and calls his cell phone number.

00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:47.654
(phone rings)

00:10:47.654 --> 00:10:49.120
- Hello, this is Tim.

00:10:50.187 --> 00:10:51.988
- [Narrator] Tim, a repentant
conman

00:10:51.988 --> 00:10:54.921
with a history of business scams
answers.

00:10:54.921 --> 00:10:57.287
And Cox asks him about his
involvement

00:10:57.287 --> 00:11:01.988
in a scene in the bank just a
week ago with Gloria McClain.

00:11:01.988 --> 00:11:04.988
Tim is surprised to be
asked about the incident.

00:11:04.988 --> 00:11:07.554
Detective Cox asks him
if he would be willing

00:11:07.554 --> 00:11:11.021
to come down to the police
station for an interview.

00:11:11.021 --> 00:11:13.354
- Yeah, that's a problem.

00:11:13.354 --> 00:11:16.621
Currently I'm unable to
move or, and/or walk.

00:11:16.621 --> 00:11:19.253
- [Narrator] When Cox presses as
to why.

00:11:19.253 --> 00:11:22.954
Tim explains that after he
exploded on Gloria in the bank,

00:11:22.954 --> 00:11:25.387
he was so angry on his drive
home

00:11:25.387 --> 00:11:27.787
that he got into a massive car
wreck

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:30.387
that broke both of his legs.

00:11:30.387 --> 00:11:34.354
He says he will be in the
hospital for a few weeks

00:11:34.354 --> 00:11:37.654
and will be unable to drive
due to his broken legs

00:11:37.654 --> 00:11:39.487
and lack of car.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.887
Cox looks up Tim's medical
records from the nearby hospital

00:11:43.887 --> 00:11:47.520
to discover that his story is
true.

00:11:49.787 --> 00:11:51.621
- What they thought was
a break in the case,

00:11:51.621 --> 00:11:54.487
turned out to be just another
dead end.

00:11:54.487 --> 00:11:56.187
If this guy was in the hospital

00:11:56.187 --> 00:11:58.554
the day after his fight with
Gloria,

00:11:58.554 --> 00:12:01.554
how can he be responsible
for her disappearance?

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:02.387
I mean, look at the guy,

00:12:02.387 --> 00:12:03.821
he's got broken legs.
- Ow!

00:12:03.821 --> 00:12:06.621
- He's got no mobility, he can't
drive.

00:12:06.621 --> 00:12:08.054
He could have nothing to do with
it.

00:12:08.054 --> 00:12:10.354
And if he had dumped it in the
park,

00:12:10.354 --> 00:12:13.021
somebody might've noticed a
hospital bed.

00:12:15.387 --> 00:12:16.921
(phone ringing)

00:12:16.921 --> 00:12:20.021
- [Narrator] Then, another
anonymous call comes in

00:12:20.021 --> 00:12:25.021
with a new tip, a new suitcase
has arrived in Memorial Park.

00:12:30.354 --> 00:12:32.554
Detective Cox finds the suitcase

00:12:32.554 --> 00:12:35.420
on the other side of
the park, under a tree,

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:39.320
a long shot away from
where they found the torso.

00:12:40.287 --> 00:12:43.387
Preparing for the worst,
police open the case,

00:12:43.387 --> 00:12:47.621
rearing back at the
sickening smell of two arms

00:12:47.621 --> 00:12:50.120
cut off at the shoulders.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.687
Cox is quick to get the parts to
the lab

00:12:52.687 --> 00:12:55.287
as they have to make sure that
the arms

00:12:55.287 --> 00:12:59.021
are a match with the torso
they found days earlier.

00:12:59.021 --> 00:13:00.754
- No prints could be taken

00:13:00.754 --> 00:13:04.320
because whoever did this
burned the fingerprints off.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.420
The first thing you wanna do
though

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.754
is match that arm to that torso.

00:13:09.754 --> 00:13:13.887
Because if they don't match,
you don't have one dead body,

00:13:13.887 --> 00:13:16.387
you have parts of two.

00:13:16.387 --> 00:13:18.487
- [Narrator] A blood match
confirms that the arms

00:13:18.487 --> 00:13:22.120
and the leg do in fact belong to
the torso

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.954
discovered days before.

00:13:23.954 --> 00:13:26.420
But the question of who
the torso belongs to

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.621
still hangs in the air.

00:13:28.621 --> 00:13:30.120
To make matters worse,

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.120
police have still been
unable to find Darren Tooley

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.320
who is now the investigation's
only notable suspect.

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:44.520
As Detective Cox is about to
head home for the evening,

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.088
she is stopped by a man

00:13:46.088 --> 00:13:48.687
who has just entered the police
station.

00:13:48.687 --> 00:13:52.587
He said that he desperately
needs to speak with police

00:13:52.587 --> 00:13:56.621
and he's carrying a suitcase.

00:13:58.021 --> 00:14:01.520
The man in the police
station identifies himself

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.320
as Darren Tooley.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:06.654
The man police assume is having
an affair

00:14:06.654 --> 00:14:08.587
with Gloria McClain.

00:14:08.587 --> 00:14:12.554
Darren claims beat just got
back from an artistic journey

00:14:12.554 --> 00:14:16.354
in the wilderness, and
that when he returned home,

00:14:16.354 --> 00:14:20.287
a suitcase was waiting on his
doorstep.

00:14:20.287 --> 00:14:23.387
He says he has not yet opened
the suitcase

00:14:23.387 --> 00:14:26.054
but his wife told him to
immediately come

00:14:26.054 --> 00:14:29.621
to the police station in
order to clear things up.

00:14:31.621 --> 00:14:33.687
Detective Cox interrogates
Darren

00:14:33.687 --> 00:14:37.454
while her forensic team
analyzes the suitcase.

00:14:37.454 --> 00:14:40.187
When they open it, they discover
a leg

00:14:40.187 --> 00:14:42.621
that is cut off at the hip.

00:14:42.621 --> 00:14:45.621
In the interrogation room,
Darren repeats his claim

00:14:45.621 --> 00:14:49.120
that he was waltzing around in
the wilderness the past week,

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.287
and that he hadn't talked
to Gloria in nearly a month.

00:14:53.287 --> 00:14:54.954
- Darren's alibi is convenient.

00:14:54.954 --> 00:14:57.021
In fact, it's too convenient.

00:14:57.021 --> 00:15:00.787
Try walking into a police
station and telling the
detective,

00:15:00.787 --> 00:15:02.687
I couldn't have been
involved in the murder

00:15:02.687 --> 00:15:07.253
because I was out alone in
nature, getting inspiration.

00:15:07.253 --> 00:15:10.220
This is the look you'll see
on the detective's face.

00:15:11.921 --> 00:15:13.954
- [Narrator] To get an
interrogative advantage,

00:15:13.954 --> 00:15:17.520
Detective Cox has her
team bring in the contents

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.387
of Darren's suitcase.

00:15:19.387 --> 00:15:22.420
Darren is appalled to see the
body parts

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:26.253
and immediately turns pale
white.

00:15:26.253 --> 00:15:28.921
His story quickly changes.

00:15:29.921 --> 00:15:33.153
Darren admits that he wasn't
in the wilderness the past week

00:15:33.153 --> 00:15:36.854
but he also didn't kill or
kidnap anyone.

00:15:36.854 --> 00:15:38.954
He had spent the last week
living

00:15:38.954 --> 00:15:42.887
with a different girlfriend
at her apartment in Chicago.

00:15:42.887 --> 00:15:46.153
He claims he broke up
with Gloria a month before

00:15:46.153 --> 00:15:47.687
because he was worried

00:15:47.687 --> 00:15:50.287
she would find out
about his new girlfriend

00:15:50.287 --> 00:15:53.487
and that Gloria would tell his
wife Joanna

00:15:53.487 --> 00:15:55.954
about his many affairs.

00:15:55.954 --> 00:15:59.687
- It's a very damning story,
but not anything beyond

00:15:59.687 --> 00:16:02.621
what someone would say to
get out of prison for murder.

00:16:02.621 --> 00:16:06.120
I'm just gonna give you
one word, corroboration.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.287
Somebody's got to corroborate
it.

00:16:09.287 --> 00:16:12.621
- Okay, I'll even give you her
number.

00:16:12.621 --> 00:16:14.854
- [Narrator] Darren gives
Cox the phone number

00:16:14.854 --> 00:16:17.687
of his Chicago girlfriend
Rebecca.

00:16:17.687 --> 00:16:19.821
Detective Cox calls Rebecca

00:16:19.821 --> 00:16:22.887
and is told that Darren's story
is true.

00:16:23.787 --> 00:16:26.587
But Detective Cox wants more
evidence.

00:16:26.587 --> 00:16:29.721
Anyone can have a friend lie for
you.

00:16:29.721 --> 00:16:33.120
She asks if Darren has a
receipt for his plane ticket,

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.021
but Darren gets quiet.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.988
- You're seeing another girl?

00:16:37.988 --> 00:16:41.887
- [Narrator] Darren explains
that a different girlfriend

00:16:41.887 --> 00:16:44.454
bought him the plane ticket to
Chicago.

00:16:44.454 --> 00:16:45.954
- This unbelievable,

00:16:45.954 --> 00:16:49.088
I mean, how many girlfriends
does this guy have?

00:16:49.088 --> 00:16:51.420
I can imagine the police are
probably in there saying,

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.021
I hope it's this guy

00:16:53.021 --> 00:16:55.220
'cause I wanna put this
sleazeball away.

00:16:56.054 --> 00:16:57.954
- [Narrator] Detective
Cox allows Darren to call

00:16:57.954 --> 00:17:01.887
his third girlfriend and an
email receipt

00:17:01.887 --> 00:17:05.120
of his plane ticket is
sent to Cox's account.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.320
- You can go.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:07.153
- Yeah.

00:17:09.021 --> 00:17:10.153
- [Narrator] With another lead

00:17:10.153 --> 00:17:12.487
effectively flushed down the
toilet,

00:17:12.487 --> 00:17:16.454
Detectives are stumped
at where to turn next.

00:17:16.454 --> 00:17:19.754
They decide to set their
sights on the only other person

00:17:19.754 --> 00:17:21.921
they believe could be involved,

00:17:21.921 --> 00:17:24.021
Gloria's brother, Paul.

00:17:27.454 --> 00:17:29.487
- Looking for my sister, my
sister Gloria,

00:17:29.487 --> 00:17:31.454
who's still missing.

00:17:31.454 --> 00:17:34.420
- [Narrator] Detective Cox
finds Paul out about town,

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.988
making a video plea for
the people of Appleton

00:17:37.988 --> 00:17:40.487
to be on the lookout for Gloria.

00:17:40.487 --> 00:17:45.253
In his arms, missing flyers
that have been stapled all over.

00:17:45.253 --> 00:17:47.287
Paul explains to Detective Cox

00:17:47.287 --> 00:17:51.420
that he has been putting up
flyers after class, every day.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.754
Detective Cox asks Paul if he
would be willing to come in

00:17:54.754 --> 00:17:56.587
and answer a few more questions.

00:17:56.587 --> 00:18:00.021
- I don't understand why, why
can't you just ask me here?

00:18:00.021 --> 00:18:00.954
- [Cox] 'Cause I cannot.

00:18:00.954 --> 00:18:03.253
- [Narrator] Paul flips into a
rage.

00:18:03.253 --> 00:18:06.787
He screams that no one
is taking him seriously.

00:18:06.787 --> 00:18:11.153
And that interrogating him is
a waste of time and resources.

00:18:11.153 --> 00:18:14.287
In his anger, he throws down the
flyers.

00:18:14.287 --> 00:18:17.153
Detective Cox becomes even more
suspicious

00:18:17.153 --> 00:18:19.021
about Paul's outbursts.

00:18:19.021 --> 00:18:21.887
- It's not normal for an
innocent person to flip out

00:18:21.887 --> 00:18:24.420
when they're asked to
assist in an investigation.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:28.054
And when that happens,
it raises a red flag.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.787
- [Narrator] Detective Cox
finally manages to convince Paul

00:18:31.787 --> 00:18:33.520
to come in for questioning,

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:36.487
though, Paul says he will only
do so

00:18:36.487 --> 00:18:39.787
if he is allowed to drop
off his things at home.

00:18:39.787 --> 00:18:42.787
Cox reassures him that
his personal possessions

00:18:42.787 --> 00:18:47.153
will be just fine as she
leads him to her cruiser.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:54.054
As they enter the station,

00:18:54.054 --> 00:18:56.787
Paul asks if his bag will be
searched

00:18:56.787 --> 00:19:00.988
as is the usual protocol
at a police station,

00:19:00.988 --> 00:19:05.120
but Detective Cox says she
will let it slide this once,

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.821
hoping to gain his trust back.

00:19:07.821 --> 00:19:10.220
Detective Cox instructs another
detective

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:12.253
to take the bag into the
evidence room

00:19:12.253 --> 00:19:15.921
but not to open it until she
gets permission from Paul

00:19:15.921 --> 00:19:19.187
because she needs a warrant
to do so on her own.

00:19:20.088 --> 00:19:21.454
In the interrogation room,

00:19:21.454 --> 00:19:24.287
Paul is visibly nervous and
shaken.

00:19:24.287 --> 00:19:27.187
Cox recalls that every
time she has seen Paul

00:19:27.187 --> 00:19:30.520
he has been dragging
his backpack behind him.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.320
Paul confirms that he
has a rolling backpack

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:34.721
due to his back injury.

00:19:34.721 --> 00:19:37.988
And every time he has seen
Detective Cox,

00:19:37.988 --> 00:19:41.220
it has been after he
has finished up a class,

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:44.187
but Detective Cox brings up
something

00:19:44.187 --> 00:19:46.153
that Paul hadn't mentioned

00:19:46.153 --> 00:19:48.721
when she was visiting their
house.

00:19:48.721 --> 00:19:52.253
The past week was also the
local community college's

00:19:52.253 --> 00:19:56.520
spring break, meaning that he
was lying.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:20:00.354
Paul turns pale white,
Detective Cox asks Paul

00:20:00.354 --> 00:20:02.988
if he's hiding anything in the
bag

00:20:02.988 --> 00:20:05.654
he has been carrying around.

00:20:06.654 --> 00:20:11.320
With a heavy sigh, Paul agrees
to allow the forensic team

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.554
to look through his backpack.

00:20:13.554 --> 00:20:16.153
Detective Cox gives them the
go-ahead

00:20:16.153 --> 00:20:19.088
to check the bag that
Paul has been guarding

00:20:19.088 --> 00:20:19.921
so suspiciously.

00:20:25.054 --> 00:20:27.954
The forensic team opens Paul's
bag

00:20:27.954 --> 00:20:31.387
to find a terrible sight.

00:20:31.387 --> 00:20:34.687
Gloria McClain's head.

00:20:34.687 --> 00:20:36.921
- Okay, I did it.

00:20:36.921 --> 00:20:38.420
- [Narrator] Paul confesses.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.887
The people of Appleton knew
the bright side of Gloria

00:20:41.887 --> 00:20:44.921
but they didn't know her dark
side.

00:20:44.921 --> 00:20:48.487
And that she was prone
to violent outbursts.

00:20:48.487 --> 00:20:51.687
The night of her disappearance,
she came home from work

00:20:51.687 --> 00:20:53.687
and flew into a rage,

00:20:53.687 --> 00:20:57.420
blaming Paul that he was the
reason Darren dumped her.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.253
- You ruined my freaking
life, Paul, Seriously.

00:21:00.253 --> 00:21:02.587
Darren left me, mom and dad are
dead.

00:21:02.587 --> 00:21:04.787
I have nothing but you.

00:21:04.787 --> 00:21:06.921
- [Narrator] She claimed
that Paul was responsible

00:21:06.921 --> 00:21:09.587
for everything horrible in her
life,

00:21:09.587 --> 00:21:13.988
and even leered out and
smacked Paul across the face.

00:21:13.988 --> 00:21:16.821
In his own fit of rage,
Paul struck his sister

00:21:16.821 --> 00:21:19.721
in the back of her head, killing
her.

00:21:19.721 --> 00:21:24.054
Instantly regretting his
actions, he cut her body up

00:21:24.054 --> 00:21:26.721
and placed them in old
suitcases,

00:21:26.721 --> 00:21:31.387
dropping them off around the
town and at Darren's house,

00:21:31.387 --> 00:21:35.587
hoping to implicate him
as the real murderer.

00:21:35.587 --> 00:21:40.120
- Every once in a while, a
case is so bizarre, so unreal,

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:43.754
so inhuman, that it shows once
again,

00:21:43.754 --> 00:21:46.220
that truth is stranger than
fiction.

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.721
(perky music)

